<title>SINGAPORE: Shell Singapore shuts 10,000T a day cracker-source.</title>
<headline>Shell Singapore shuts 10,000T a day cracker-source.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell Singapore had over the weekend shutdown a 10,000-11,000 tonne per day cracking unit, sources close to the company said on Monday.</p>
<p>The unit is expected to be closed for about one week, the source said. The source was not able to confirm the reason for the shutdown.</p>
<p>The unit cracks heavy residual fuel to produce between 30 and 40 percent of middle distillate and fuel oil making up the rest.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3093)</p>
</text>
